A||N||9||acecabo||Ground Up Fiero to Diablo build.||||5||
Z||000000||acecabo||10-18-2001||03:15 PM||||Hi all u fiero lovers out there. I recently got a wild hair to build a Diablo from a 88 fiero. I have the doner with no drivetrain and no body. I need help on how to rebuild the fiero to show quality and what engine/tranny/drivetrain to get 450-600 hp out of it (turbo of cource). Any information would help. IE start by cleaning up the frame, replace rusted parts. next upgrade the brakes, next blah blah and so forth. I appreaite all help.<BR>carl||||reg||5
Z||000001||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-18-2001||03:25 PM||||This site should help you out a little on info..<BR> <A HREF="http://home.pacbell.net/oohec/main.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.pacbell.net/oohec/main.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||10-18-2001||04:19 PM||||Well, just start stripping and cleaning the chassis.  As to the engine- check with archie at <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.v8archie.com</A> <P>Welcome to the forum- and good luck with your project.  You've definitely got your work cut out for you!<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||acecabo||10-18-2001||04:28 PM||||I've been to archie's site before, and actually was thinkin of getting a kit from him. but seeing all the 3800 conversions merits the question...which will be better for me. IE, which has a better hp to torque to weight ratio? a lighter v6 with turbo or a heavier v8 with more torque? i want a rocketship here..i drive a 225hp eclipse at the moment and its not fast enough.<BR>thanks again||||reg||1
Z||000004||MinnGreenGT||10-18-2001||04:56 PM||||If you want true power, you can't beat the torque and power of a V8. (Archie Rules!)  The 3800 Series II S/C engine is great (I'd love to have one), but I think it would take quite a bit more work (intercooler, underdrive pulleys, etc...) to get the 3800 above 400hp, whereas a SBC is not far from there to start.  A set of performance heads/intake/exhaust, and maybe a little bottle of N20 and you'll be well on your way past 400hp.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jason Kalbfleisch||10-18-2001||11:31 PM||||Good luck with your Diablo.I would advise you to really put some thought into this project.Find someone in your area who is building a kit of any kind.It is an enormous undertaking,mentally,physically,and financially.Do not even think about starting it unless you can devote nearly 100% of your spare time to it.||||reg||1
Z||000006||onfire||10-19-2001||03:22 AM||||Also check this guys website out.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.lambobuilder.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.lambobuilder.com/</A> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/onfiresigtoo.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||10-19-2001||09:10 AM||||Your going to have trouble finding that kind of HP in a street car. Even Vette Z06 only has 400. Dont think you can squeeze a Viper V10 in a Fiero either. Im currently working on getting a Countach kit, partially done with Olds 455 about 350 hp.||||reg||1
